    {
      "title": "HTTP Clients: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "HTTP Clients: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Two Clients",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==RestClient== (Spring 6.1+): **synchronous**, fluent, replaces `RestTemplate` in new code",
                "==WebClient== (spring-webflux): non-blocking, returns `Mono` / `Flux`",
                "WebClient sends ==nothing== until you subscribe",
                "`.block()` is the escape hatch to wait for the result"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "RestClient rc = RestClient.builder()",
                "    .baseUrl(\"https://api.example.com\")",
                "    .build();"
              ],
              "note": "or inject the auto-configured RestClient.Builder"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Which One to Use",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "RestClient",
                "WebClient",
                "RestTemplate"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Model",
                  "Blocks a thread",
                  "Reactive",
                  "Blocks a thread"
                ],
                [
                  "Suits",
                  "MVC, virtual threads",
                  "Streaming, high fan-out",
                  "{red:Maintenance mode}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Build and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Build from the ==injected Builder==, not a bare `new`",
                "Boot's message converters, observability and customizers then apply"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`block()` inside a reactive pipeline",
                "A new client per request: throws away the ==connection pool=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Build once, reuse",
              "text": "One client per remote service, built from the injected Builder and kept as a **bean**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Making Calls and Declarative HTTP Interfaces",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Making Calls and Declarative HTTP Interfaces",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Fluent calls",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Chain ==retrieve()== then pick the body type",
                "Generics need `ParameterizedTypeReference`",
                "`toEntity(User.class)` when you need status or headers"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "client.get().uri(\"/users/{id}\", id).retrieve().body(User.class);",
                "client.get().uri(\"/users\").retrieve()",
                "  .body(new ParameterizedTypeReference<List<User>>(){});",
                "client.post().uri(\"/users\").contentType(APPLICATION_JSON)",
                "  .body(dto).retrieve().toBodilessEntity();"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Want",
                "RestClient",
                "WebClient"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "One value",
                  "`body(User.class)`",
                  "`bodyToMono(User.class)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Stream",
                  "n/a",
                  "`bodyToFlux(User.class)`"
                ],
                [
                  "No body",
                  "`toBodilessEntity()`",
                  "`toBodilessEntity()`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Declarative interface",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==@HttpExchange(\"/users\")== on the interface",
                "Methods: `@GetExchange`, `@PostExchange`",
                "Params: `@PathVariable`, `@RequestParam`, `@RequestBody`",
                "Adapter can wrap a `WebClient` instead: `WebClientAdapter`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "@HttpExchange(\"/users\")",
                "interface UserApi {",
                "  @GetExchange(\"/{id}\") User get(@PathVariable long id);",
                "}",
                "@Bean UserApi userApi(RestClient rc) {",
                "  return HttpServiceProxyFactory",
                "    .builderFor(RestClientAdapter.create(rc))",
                "    .build().createClient(UserApi.class); }"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake",
              "text": "The interface is only a **proxy**. No adapter or no @Bean registration means ==no bean== to inject."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Timeouts and Error Handling for Outbound Calls",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Timeouts and Error Handling for Outbound Calls",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Always Set Timeouts",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Defaults are effectively ==unbounded==",
                "Set a **connect** and a **read** timeout on every client",
                "No timeout: one slow dependency ==exhausts the thread pool=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Configuring Them",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "RestClient",
                "WebClient"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Connect",
                  "`HttpClient.newBuilder().connectTimeout(...)`",
                  "`option(CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MILLIS, 2000)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Read",
                  "`setReadTimeout(...)`",
                  "`responseTimeout(Duration.ofSeconds(3))`"
                ],
                [
                  "Wrapper",
                  "`JdkClientHttpRequestFactory`",
                  "`ReactorClientHttpConnector`"
                ],
                [
                  "Other",
                  "Boot `spring.http.client.connect-timeout`, `read-timeout`",
                  "per-call `.timeout(Duration)` on the Mono"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "var http = HttpClient.newBuilder().connectTimeout(Duration.ofSeconds(2)).build();",
                "var f = new JdkClientHttpRequestFactory(http);",
                "f.setReadTimeout(Duration.ofSeconds(3));",
                "var client = RestClient.builder().requestFactory(f).build();"
              ],
              "note": "RestClient: timeouts live on the request factory"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Errors and Retries",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Client",
                "retrieve() throws on 4xx / 5xx"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "RestClient",
                  "`HttpClientErrorException`, `HttpServerErrorException` (both `RestClientResponseException`)"
                ],
                [
                  "WebClient",
                  "`WebClientResponseException`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Customize: `.onStatus(HttpStatusCode::is4xxClientError, (req, res) -> { throw new MyException(res.getStatusCode()); })`",
                "{red:Blind retry} of non-idempotent ==POST==",
                "Catching generic `Exception` hides the status",
                "WebClient: `retryWhen(Retry.backoff(3, Duration.ofMillis(200)))`, idempotent and transient only"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Kafka Producers and @KafkaListener Consumers",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Kafka Producers and @KafkaListener Consumers",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Producer",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`send(topic, key, value)` on `KafkaTemplate<String,Order>` returns a ==CompletableFuture== (non-blocking)",
                "Same ==key== → same partition → per-key order",
                "{red:Null key}: spread across partitions, no ordering",
                "`acks=all` + `enable.idempotence=true`: no loss or duplicates on retry",
                "Set `spring.kafka.producer.key-serializer` and `value-serializer` (`JsonSerializer`)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "kafka.send(\"orders\", o.id(), o)",
                "  .whenComplete((r, ex) -> {",
                "    if (ex != null) log.error(\"failed\", ex);",
                "  });"
              ],
              "note": "log failures in whenComplete"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Consumer",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`@KafkaListener` on a method; one ==group== splits the partitions",
                "{green:Different groups} each get every record",
                "Concurrency above the partition count = ==idle== consumers"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "@KafkaListener(topics = \"orders\", groupId = \"billing\")",
                "void on(Order o) { bill(o); }"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Offsets and Mistakes",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Manual control: `spring.kafka.listener.ack-mode=manual`, take an `Acknowledgment ack`, call `ack.acknowledge()`",
                "New group: set `auto.offset.reset=earliest`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "AckMode",
                "Commits"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`BATCH` (default)",
                  "after the poll batch is processed"
                ],
                [
                  "`MANUAL`",
                  "when you call `acknowledge()`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Slow listener passes `max.poll.interval.ms` → rebalance; speed it up or lower `max.poll.records`",
                "JSON rejected unless `spring.json.trusted.packages` is set to your package"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Retries and Dead-Letter Topics",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Retries and Dead-Letter Topics",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Blocking Retries and the DLT",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Default `DefaultErrorHandler`: ==10 delivery attempts== (first + 9 retries), no delay, then log and skip",
                "`FixedBackOff(1000L, 3)` = first delivery + ==3 retries==, 1 s apart; or `ExponentialBackOff`",
                "`DeadLetterPublishingRecoverer` sends the record to ==<topic>.DLT==, same partition, error in headers",
                "Skip retries for bad data with `addNotRetryableExceptions(...)`",
                "Wrap the deserializer in ==ErrorHandlingDeserializer==: a poison message goes to the DLT, no endless loop"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "@Bean",
                "DefaultErrorHandler errorHandler(KafkaTemplate<String, Order> t) {",
                "  var back = new FixedBackOff(1000L, 3);",
                "  var h = new DefaultErrorHandler(new DeadLetterPublishingRecoverer(t), back);",
                "  h.addNotRetryableExceptions(ValidationException.class);",
                "  return h;",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "retry 3 times, then publish to orders.DLT"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Non-Blocking Retries",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "orders",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "orders-retry-0",
                    "sub": "1 s",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "orders-retry-1",
                    "sub": "2 s",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "orders-retry-2",
                    "sub": "4 s",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "orders-dlt",
                    "sub": "@DltHandler",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`@RetryableTopic(attempts=\"4\", backoff=@Backoff(delay=1000, multiplier=2))`",
                "{green:Pro:} the partition is not stalled while a record waits",
                "{red:Con:} ordering is broken"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Retrying forever on a permanent failure",
                "Non-idempotent listeners: delivery is ==at-least-once==, so duplicates happen",
                "Never monitoring or replaying the DLT"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cheat Sheet: Clients and Kafka",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cheat Sheet: Clients and Kafka",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Clients and Timeouts",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Client",
                "Style",
                "Pick for"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`RestClient`",
                  "sync",
                  "MVC"
                ],
                [
                  "`WebClient`",
                  "reactive",
                  "streaming"
                ],
                [
                  "`@HttpExchange` + `HttpServiceProxyFactory`",
                  "typed proxy",
                  "declarative calls"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "User u = restClient.get().uri(\"/users/{id}\", id)",
                "    .retrieve().body(User.class);",
                "Mono<User> m = webClient.get().uri(\"/users/{id}\", id)",
                "    .retrieve().bodyToMono(User.class);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Build from the injected ==Builder==",
                "`retrieve()` throws on 4xx/5xx: use `onStatus`",
                "Set ==connect + read timeouts==: default is unbounded",
                "Retry only ==idempotent== calls, with backoff"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Kafka Send and Consume",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "kafkaTemplate.send(\"orders\", key, order); // future",
                "",
                "@KafkaListener(topics = \"orders\", groupId = \"billing\")",
                "void on(Order o) { }"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Key== picks the partition: sets ordering",
                "`acks=all` + idempotence on",
                "Same group shares partitions; other groups get all records",
                "Concurrency capped by ==partition count=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Errors",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Listener throws",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "DefaultErrorHandler",
                    "sub": "BackOff",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "DeadLetterPublishingRecoverer",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "orders.DLT",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Delivery is at-least-once: keep consumers ==idempotent==. `ErrorHandlingDeserializer` catches bad payloads; `@RetryableTopic` retries without blocking."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
